4. helper/simd.swift, helper/simd.h: mostly original work for this mod, under the MIT License like
   the rest of it. simd.swift also holds the serve-sim portions listed in entry 5, which stay under
   the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE), and the herdr-sim Android frame parse in
   entry 6. Both files call Apple's private CoreSimulator and SimulatorKit frameworks shipped with
   Xcode; the few declarations in simd.h were taken from those frameworks' own runtime class
   metadata.

5. serve-sim 0.1.49 by Evan Bacon (https://github.com/EvanBacon/serve-sim), Apache License,
   Version 2.0. The author is named in the package's package.json; the package has no copyright
   line or NOTICE file of its own. The full license text is in LICENSE-APACHE. Adapted, and
   modified for drover-sim:
   - helper/simd.swift: the touch phase mapping (a move is sent as Down), the IndigoHIDEdge
     values, scroll as a one-finger drag with edge re-anchoring, and the Device Hub input repair
     sequence.
   - lib/devicehub.js: the Device Hub notify key, the shadowed check and the repair order.
   - lib/throttle.js: wheelToScroll's web wheel sign and pointer anchor, the shape the
     scroll-as-drag takes.

6. herdr-sim by Robert Soriano (https://github.com/wobsoriano/herdr-sim), MIT License. Adapted,
   and modified for drover-sim:
   - lib/ring.js: the frame ring with a delayed reveal, the due-time gate and one slot set per
     view.
   - lib/coords.js: touchEdge's HOME_BAND 0.93 rule for the bottom edge.
   - helper/simd.swift: the Android frame source, i.e. the ImageFormat protobuf request and the
     Image.image (field 4) extraction for streamScreenshot, rewritten in Swift.
   - main.js: the stacked image render, so a frame is decoded before it is on top.
   - lib/sim.js: the Android input argument shapes (motionevent DOWN/MOVE/UP with moves
     coalesced, the swipe ... 120 wheel, the USB usage to Android keycode table and
     keycombination 59 for Shift). herdr-sim runs adb through sh -c; here each one is an argv.

